SUMMARY:FYI: What’s happenin’
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nFor Oct 8 thru Oct 14\n\nUpcoming **music e
 vents** may be found here:\nhttps://www.facebook.com/hendolivemusic/\n(Upd
 ates on Thurs morning)\n\n**Assorted entertainment\, festival & market eve
 nts may be found here:**\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.org/calendar-of-ev
 ents\n\n**Library programs** may be found here:\nhttps://hendersonpl.libca
 l.com/\n\n**FYI: Rockin’ on the Rock**\nOctober 9\, 2026\n5pm / Free\nJu
 mp Off Rock\, Laurel Park\, NC\nEnjoy live music at the picturesque Jump O
 ff Rock\, which overlooks the French Broad River valley and the Blue Ridge
  Mountains beyond. Musical offerings ranging from jazz to country\, rockab
 illy\, pop\, rock and blues. Organized by the Friends of Laurel Park.\nOct
  9\; 5:00 pm\; Rockin’ on the Rock with Autumnwood\nJump Off Rock\; 4433
  Laurel Park Hwy\, Laurel Park\, NC 28739\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.o
 rg/event/rockin-on-the-rock-with-autumnwood\n\n**October 9** @ 6:00 pm - 8
 :00 pm\; Free\nHallow’d Art Show Opening\nStudio 116 presents Hallow’d
  Art Show\, a community exhibition celebrating the mysterious\, imaginativ
 e\, and meaningful side of the season where artists explore themes of reme
 mbrance\, folklore\, spirits\, and the traditions that surround this time 
 of year. Hallow’d Art Show runs October 9–31\nhttps://visithendersonvi
 llenc.org/event/hallowd-art-show-opening\n\n**Friday\, October 9**\nSOUTHE
 RN APPALACHIAN BREWERY \\* The Mattocks-Johnson Band (blues / classic rock
 ) \\* 7:00 – 9:00\n\n**Friday\, October 9**\nBlake Anthony Ellege & The 
 Big Throwback\n8pm\, Oklawaha Brewery\, 147 First Ave East\, Hendersonvill
 e\n\n**Saturday\, October 10**\nBarktober at Booda-fest\; 12:30 pm - 5 pm.
 \na charity event supporting the local Blue Ridge Humane Society. There wi
 ll be local vendors with products for you and your pets and lots of activi
 ties for every age. Stein holding contest at 3:00pm and best dressed leder
 hosen contest at 4:00pm. Bring the pups and friends!!\nBoodas brewing\; 12
 0 E Barnwell St\, Hendersonville\,\n\n**Saturday\, October 10**\nOklawaha 
 brewing co. \\* oktoberfest & block party!\n1:30 \\* TrancEnd\; 7:00 \\* R
 andomonium\n\n**Saturday\, October 10**\nBeach Night With DJ Dave Hadden (
 This event is open to the public)\n6:15-10pm\, American Legion Post 77\, 2
 16 4th Avenue West\, Hendersonville NC 28739\n6:15-7pm - Cy Miller and Joy
 ce Anderson will teach a shag step. 7-10pm - Shag Dance.\nThe dance entry 
 door is upstairs off of the upper parking lot. Dave plays a great variety 
 of music that\nincludes swing\, shag\, some cha-chas\, rhumbas and a line 
 dance or two. Bring a partner or come solo.\nFull Bar and kitchen availabl
 e with Free Parking in the upper lot. Cost: $7 per person (Cash only).\n\n
 **Sunday\, Oct 11**\nHendersonville Ballroom Dance Club Tea Dance - **Atti
 re: Lots of Bling**\n3-5_30pm\, Upstairs at Hedrick Rhodes Veterans Center
 \, 900 North Main St\, Hendersonville\n3pm – American Tango Dance Lesson
  with Carrie Fernandez.\nOpen Ballroom Dance to the music of DJ Gary Bills
 . Ample parking at the front entry of the building\, take the elevator or 
 stairs to the upper level. Parking is limited at the rear entrance\, both 
 front and back doors will be unlocked. Our dances are open to the public a
 nd everyone is invited. Enjoy Ballroom Dancing to dance tunes including Sw
 ing (East & West Coast)\, Waltz\, Tango\, Rumba\, Cha-Cha and Foxtrot. The
 re is also a dance mixer. Cost: $5 per person at door.\n**Next Dance 10/25
 **\n\n**Tue\; Oct 13**\nDancing the night away..\nLine dancing\, Swing\, B
 allroom and more.\n6-8 PM – FREE\nFirst United Methodist Church\n204 6th
  Ave West\; Hendersonville\nThe night will start with a Line Dance Lesson 
 followed by open dancing.\nThey will have free refreshments and tables and
  chairs will be set up. All you need is your dancing shoes.\nParking is in
  the rear of the church and enter through the double doors.\nFor more info
 : Michael Brannon\n\n**Wednesday\, October 14**\nJason DeCristofaro's Jazz
  Night\n6-8pm\, Southern Appalachian Brewery\, 822 Locust St\, Hendersonvi
 lle\n\n**Wednesday\, October 14**\nWeekly Westie Wednesdays (Ages 21 & Up)
  (Each Wednesday)\n7-10pm\, Honeysuckle Holler\, 101 East Allen St\, Suite
  101\, Hendersonville NC 28792\n7-8pm - Continuation Lesson & 7:30-8pm - B
 eginner Lesson. 8-10pm - Social Dance.\nLessons rotate weekly with our inc
 redible instructor lineup: Ryan Pflumm\, Jason Barnes\, Jenna Shimek\,\nMi
 ssy Lindsey\, Rachel Harris\, Tom and Janet Leazenby\, and Tola Sun - all 
 bringing fresh energy and\nperspectives each week! Enjoy a rotation of com
 munity DJs keeping the vibes high and the floor full all night\nlong. No o
 utside drinks (including water bottles) - water station available. Outside
  food welcome. Dress is\ncasual and No partner needed! Dedicated parking n
 ext to the venue & street parking. Please help us\nsupport our amazing hos
 t venue by grabbing a drink or snack at the bar - it helps keep dance nigh
 ts thriving!\nPricing: $10 lesson & social\, $5 social only.\n\n**October 
 15th**\n**Rhythm & Brews:**\n5:30 pm - 9:00 pm\; Free\nhttps://visithender
 sonvillenc.org/\nPresented by Horizon Heating & Air\, Rhythm & Brews Conce
 rt Series brings together live music\, local craft beverages\, and the com
 munity! These free shows take place on the third Thursday of every month f
 rom June-October\, closing part of South Main Street to make room for all 
 the fun. Local food trucks will line the street cooking delicious eats fro
 m kettle corn to pizza to barbecue. Each show begins with an opener at 5:0
 0 p.m. followed by the headlining performance from 7:00-9:00 p.m.\n2026 Rh
 ythm & Brews Concert Series Lineup:\nOctober 15: Unspoken Tradition [[Blue
 grassl] with Finkelstein Three [[Bluegrass/Jazzgrass]]\nOpening acts will 
 kick off each evening at 5 p.m. followed by the headliner performance from
  7-9 p.m.\n\n**October 16 thru 18th\; 10a - 4p**\n***Open Studio Tour 2026
 ***\nFor one weekend\, visitors will have the opportunity to meet artists 
 where they create\, see works in progress\, learn about different creative
  processes\, and discover original artwork and handmade pieces throughout 
 the region. While the tour is rooted in Henderson County\, some participat
 ing artists have studios just beyond the county line.\nhttps://www.studio1
 16nc.com/studiotour\n***Maps & locations TBD***\n\n**October 18** @ 3:00 p
 m - 5:00 pm\; $12\nThe Hendersonville Community Band will play the first c
 oncert of our new season on October 18 at 3PM at the Blue Ridge Community 
 College. Theme is Fall Colors. There will be a variety of selections. We w
 ill feature Furman University student Jillian Hansard – a clarinet soloi
 st & Hendersonville Community Band scholarship winner on “Clarinet Candy
 ”. Holst’s “Second Suite in F”\, Clifton Williams’s “Symphonic
  Suite”\, “Pixar Movie Magic”\, John Williams’s “Chillers and Th
 rillers” (Halloween!)\, Sousa’s march “The Thunderer” (with guest 
 conductor Mr. James Phillips from Hendersonville High School). Lastly\, a 
 trumpet trio on “Carnival Variations” – something for everyone! Adva
 nce tickets available at Hendersonville Visitors Center. Tickets are $12 (
 students free) and also available at door.\nhttps://visithendersonvillenc.
 org/event/hendersonville-community-band-fall-colors-concert\n\nThese are N
 OT hosted events and are posted for informational purposes only. Please ma
 ke personal arrangements to meetup with friends and family.\nIf you wish t
 o attend and host one of these events\, I will post the event as an indivi
 dual happening. Hosting only requires being focal point for others and mak
 ing introductions. Simple!!
