SUMMARY:Buck Spring Trail\; a Saunter 
DESCRIPTION:Hendo Fun Friends\nA seasonal favorite\; this is a very pleasa
 nt hike that weaves in and out of the various coves that lie along the sou
 theast face of the mountain ridge that rises up above Pink Beds. I suggest
  extra socks & towels for any surprises on the creek Xings.\nWe will be CA
 TCHING Fall color.\nI will be carrying the ‘Ent-Ward’ that gives us pe
 rmission to pass thru the forest.\n**DIFFICULTY:** rocky & dirt narrow tra
 il. 6 moderately challenging rock-hop creek Xingsl. There may be unexpecte
 d challenges and obstacles.\n**We are the Sloth Hike Team of WNC: “We wi
 ll get there when we get there.” We dare to go where the ‘real’ hike
  groups don’t !!**\n**John Muir didn’t like the word ‘hike’. *“W
 e ought to saunter through them reverently\, not 'hike' through them.”**
 *\nDetails:\n**(Social ‘hour’ at 9:45AM. Parade leaves at 9:55AM)**\nL
 ength: 4 mi (in & out) to Picnic Rock from Hwy 276 and back.\nAccum ascent
 : 500 ft total (gradual). Pace: **1.5mph.**\n**IF YOU HAVE AN ORANGE VEST\
 ; WEAR IT. HUNTING SEASON HAS STARTED. \;-) THEY ARE INEXPENSIVE AT WALMAR
 T....**\n**Drive time: 20 min 1-way**\n**Return Not earlier than: 2 pm (=4
 hrs)**\n**Optional:** Late lunch after – at a location determined by the
  vimen….\nCarpool contributions appreciated. $2.00 suggested\n**THIS IS 
 A DOG-PARTICIPANT HIKE.** This event is NOT for those who are uncomfortabl
 e with the antics of fun-loving dogs. Well trained dogs **(you don’t hav
 e to yell)** can be 'off-leash'. 'On leash' when meeting other hikers. Sma
 ll (lap)dogs may carpool. Large dogs will drive themselves.\nIncessant pra
 ttlers will be assumed to be having an affair.\nWeather Check: Brevard\, N
 C\nWAITLISTED PEOPLE WILL BE ADDED AS DRIVERS SIGN ON.\nI currently have 1
  driver(s)\nWe suggest open windows while carpooling. Only you know your o
 wn health status so judge accordingly if an event may endanger your health
  or the health of others. Please bring an extra pair of shoes to avoid bri
 nging your muddy shoes into the driver's car at the end of the hike.\nAll 
 hikes are at your own risk. You are responsible for your OWN safety and ad
 equate equipment.\nWaiver: There are certain risks inherent in any outdoor
  activity. Each participant\, by signing up to attend this event\, agrees 
 to release from liability the leader(s)\, Hendo Fun Friends\, its Partners
 \, Affiliates\, and members for any accident\, injury\, illness\, or perso
 nal loss which might occur while participating in this activity or while t
 raveling in any vehicle during this trip. **Each participant further agree
 s to abide by the rules and regulations concerning safety\, to follow inst
 ructions of the leader(s)\, and not to become intentionally separated from
  the group.** The leader(s) also has the right to use any images collected
  on this trip for recording on website photo collections.\ngordie's contac
 t: CurmudgeonHiker@gmail.com\n(**before** day of hike): 828.393.0297 (talk
  & text)\n**Pics: https://www.flickr.com/photos/146993931@N05/albums**
